{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolumeCatalan","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolumeCatalan","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanVolumeCatalan","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_lt_vol_B3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_lt_vol_B3","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WhiteheadVolumeCatalan.lean#L97-L102","doc":"`Vol(L5a1) < Vol(𝓑₃)` — the Whitehead sits below the Borromean on the\nhyperbolic-volume ladder of Table 3 building-block links (one octahedron\nvs two). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_numerical_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_numerical_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WhiteheadVolumeCatalan.lean#L87-L95","doc":"Numerical bracket: `3.66 < Vol(L5a1) < 3.67` (from `0.915 < G < 0.916`).\nMatches the SnapPy census value `3.663862376708…` for L5a1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WhiteheadVolumeCatalan.lean#L84-L85","doc":"`Vol(L5a1) ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_pos","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WhiteheadVolumeCatalan.lean#L79-L82","doc":"`Vol(L5a1) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_eq_eight_lobachevsky","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_eq_eight_lobachevsky","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WhiteheadVolumeCatalan.lean#L71-L77","doc":"**Octahedral (Lobachevsky) form**: `Vol(L5a1) = 8·Λ(π/4)`.\n\nA single regular ideal octahedron has volume `8·Λ(π/4)`; combined with\nthe Lobachevsky–Catalan identity `Λ(π/4) = G/2` this is `4G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_eq_half_vol_B3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_eq_half_vol_B3","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WhiteheadVolumeCatalan.lean#L62-L69","doc":"**Exact half-Borromean relation**: `Vol(L5a1) = Vol(𝓑₃) / 2`.\n\nThe Whitehead complement is one regular ideal octahedron; the Borromean\ncomplement is two.  Both volumes are `catalan_G` multiples, so the\nrelation is an exact algebraic identity (`4G = 8G / 2`), proved\nsorry-free — no numerical approximation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_eq_4_catalan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1_eq_4_catalan","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WhiteheadVolumeCatalan.lean#L59-L60","doc":"`Vol(L5a1) = 4·G` — definitional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WhiteheadVolume.vol_L5a1","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WhiteheadVolumeCatalan.lean#L52-L57","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Whitehead link complement `L5a1`, as the exact\nsymbolic value `4 · G` (one regular ideal octahedron).\n\n-- Ref: [wielenberg1978] the Whitehead complement is a single regular\n        ideal octahedron; [adams1985hyperbolic] octahedron volume = 4G. ","signatureChunk":0}]}